`,wt(t.p,{children:["Motion transfer is an important task in video editing with numerous practical applications. Current leading approaches fine-tune a small scale of parameters, e.g., LoRA, on a single source video to adapt the video diffusion model (VDM) to its motion. However, such single-video fine-tuning makes it challenging to ensure the physical realism of intrinsic motion. For example, when editing a car to a horse, the LoRA tends to memorize the rotation of the car's tires, resulting in the horse's legs appearing stiff, and the overall posture is nearly unchanged. To this end, we propose a ",wt(t.strong,{children:"Dual grained Re-Adaptation Motion Transfer (DRA-MTransfer)"})," method, which utilizes the potential motion prior within the pre-trained VDM to tackle the motion constraint imposed by the source video."]}),`
